  "term": "bioenergetics",
  "definition": "Bioenergetics refers to the processes by which cells, especially mitochondria, produce and manage energy such as ATP. In this context, it is used to describe measurable patterns of cellular energy production and how these change in disease or when parts of the electron transport chain are impaired.",
